l-view-affiliation-3 \"Ocean University Medical Center\")\n\nIn: StatPearls \\[Internet\\]. Treasure Island (FL): StatPearls Publishing; 2026 Jan.\n\n2025 Dec 13.\n\nAffiliations Expand\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Einstein Medical Center\n-   2 Jefferson Einstein Medical Center\n-   3 Ocean University Medical Center\n\n-   PMID: **32965926**\n-   Bookshelf ID: [NBK562255](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/)\n\nFree Books & Documents\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nBook\n\n# Lymphocytic Hypophysitis\n\nJustin Riley Lam et al.\n\nFree Books & Documents\n\nShow details\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat Abstract PubMed PMID\n\nIn: StatPearls \\[Internet\\]. Treasure Island (FL): StatPearls Publishing; 2026 Jan.\n\n2025 Dec 13.\n\n### Authors\n\n[Justin Riley Lam](/?term=Lam+JR&cauthor_id=32965926)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Einstein Medical Center\") , [Catherine Anastasopoulou](/?term=Anastasopoulou+C&cauthor_id=32965926)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Jefferson Einstein Medical Center\") , [Ahmet S. Can](/?term=Can+AS&cauthor_id=32965926)  [3](#short-view-affiliation-3 \"Ocean University Medical Center\")\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Einstein Medical Center\n-   2 Jefferson Einstein Medical Center\n-   3 Ocean University Medical Center\n\n-   PMID: **32965926**\n-   Bookshelf ID: [NBK562255](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nFull text links Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat AbstractPubMedPMID\n\n## Excerpt\n\nLymphocytic hypophysitis is a rare inflammatory disorder of the pituitary gland that presents with features of hypopituitarism secondary to a sellar mass lesion. The condition is characterized by infiltration of the pituitary gland with T and B lymphocytes. This autoimmune condition is the most frequent histopathologic subtype of primary hypophysitis. Endocrine symptoms are due to pituitary dysfunction and may include central diabetes insipidus, anterior pituitary hormone deficiencies, hyperprolactinemia, or hypoprolactinemia.\n\nPatients may also present with symptoms of mass effect, such as headaches or visual field disturbances, which can mimic a pituitary adenoma. Early recognition is crucial for guiding appropriate hormonal replacement and preventing unnecessary surgical intervention. Because lymphocytic hypophysitis is relatively rare, diagnosis and treatment can be challenging.\n\nCopyright © 2026, StatPearls Publishing LLC.\n\n[PubMed Disclaimer](/disclaimer/)\n\n## Conflict of interest statement\n\nDisclosure: Justin Riley Lam declares no relevant financial relationships with ineligible companies.\n\nDisclosure: Catherine Anastasopoulou declares no relevant financial relationships with ineligible companies.\n\nDisclosure: Ahmet Can declares no relevant financial relationships with ineligible companies.\n\n## Sections\n\n-   [Continuing Education Activity](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s1)\n-   [Introduction](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s2)\n-   [Etiology](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s3)\n-   [Epidemiology](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s4)\n-   [Histopathology](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s5)\n-   [History and Physical](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s6)\n-   [Evaluation](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s7)\n-   [Treatment / Management](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s8)\n-   [Differential Diagnosis](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s9)\n-   [Prognosis](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s10)\n-   [Complications](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s11)\n-   [Deterrence and Patient Education](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s12)\n-   [Enhancing Healthcare Team Outcomes](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s13)\n-   [Review Questions](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s14)\n-   [References](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255/#article-24571.s17)\n\n## References\n\n1.  1.  Molitch ME, Gillam MP. Lymphocytic hypophysitis. Horm Res. 2007;68 Suppl 5:145-50. - [PubMed](/18174733/)\n2.  1.  Honegger J, Schlaffer S, Menzel C, Droste M, Werner S, Elbelt U, Strasburger C, Störmann S, Küppers A, Streetz-van der Werf C, Deutschbein T, Stieg M, Rotermund R, Milian M, Petersenn S, Pituitary Working Group of the German Society of Endocrinology Diagnosis of Primary Hypophysitis in Germany. J Clin Endocrinol Metab. 2015 Oct;100(10):3841-9. - [PubMed](/26262437/)\n3.  1.  Nanda A, Savardekar AR, Patra DP. Diagnosis and management of lymphocytic hypophysitis: A synopsis on current perspective. Neurol India. 2018 Mar-Apr;66(2):405-406. - [PubMed](/29547162/)\n4.  1.  Joshi MN, Whitelaw BC, Carroll PV. MECHANISMS IN ENDOCRINOLOGY: Hypophysitis: diagnosis and treatment. Eur J Endocrinol. 2018 Sep;179(3):R151-R163. - [PubMed](/29880706/)\n5.  1.  Patil AA, Patil P, Walke V. Lymphocytic Hypophysitis: An Underrated Disease. J Midlife Health. 2022 Jul-Sep;13(3):254-256. - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10025822/) - [PubMed](/36950203/)\n\nShow all 26 references\n\n## Publication types\n\n-   Study Guide\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Study+Guide%22%5Bpt%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Study+Guide)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n\n## LinkOut - more resources\n\n-   ### Full Text Sources\n    \n    -   [NCBI Bookshelf](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255)\n\n**Full text links** \\[x\\]\n\n[![book cover photo](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/corehtml/pmc/pmcgifs/bookshelf/thumbs/th-statpearls.png)\n\nStatPearls \\[Internet\\]\n\nNCBI Bookshelf](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562255 \"See full text op