{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979982360,"sessionID":"ses_1cc8acd6dffephn30ptdQ0bam5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_BNJq09847Gi8ZHIgEWYDlpFV","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Summary:\n+- Created a distinct `lymphocytic hypophysitis` child term under `primary hypophysitis`.\n+- Removed `lymphocytic hypophysitis` and `autoimmune hypophysitis` from the parent term where they were modeled as exact synonyms.\n+- Reparented `adenohypophysitis`, `infundibulo-neurohypophysitis`, and `panhypophysitis` under `lymphocytic hypophysitis` to match the issue discussion and cited literature.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the issue as a hierarchy correction rather than a synonym-only edit.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Added new term `MONDO:7770459` `lymphocytic hypophysitis`.\n+- Added a definition supported by `PMID:29547162` and `PMID:32965926`, both of which describe lymphocytic hypophysitis as the most frequent histopathologic subtype of primary hypophysitis.\n+- Moved the `NCIT:C132055` equivalence and the `autoimmune hypophysitis` synonym off `MONDO:0019835 primary hypophysitis` and onto the new `lymphocytic hypophysitis` term, because `NCIT:C132055` is `Autoimmune Hypophysitis` with exact synonym `Lymphocytic Hypophysitis`.\n+- Reparented these existing terms from `primary hypophysitis` to `lymphocytic hypophysitis`:\n+  - `MONDO:0019838` adenohypophysitis\n+  - `MONDO:0016534` infundibulo-neurohypophysitis\n+  - `MONDO:0019839` panhypophysitis\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue body and follow-up comment describe `primary hypophysitis` as the broader parent term.\n+- The cited sources support `lymphocytic hypophysitis` as a subtype, not as a synonym of the parent.\n+- Keeping `primary hypophysitis` aligned to its Orphanet-backed grouping concept while moving the NCIT mapping to the more specific child resolves the conceptual mismatch.\n+\n+Validation and research performed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Reviewed the cited NCBI Bookshelf page and PubMed entry for the Neurology India article.\n+- Verified that `NCIT:C132055` is labeled `Autoimmune Hypophysitis` and carries exact synonym `Lymphocytic Hypophysitis`.\n+- Verified that `MONDO:7770459` was unused before creating the new term.\n+- Checked the integrated stanzas in `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo` after check-in.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+- [x] Read issue context and comments\n+- [x] Reviewed cited references\n+- [x] Identified affected MONDO terms\n+- [x] Added a new subtype term with supporting references\n+- [x] Reparented existing anatomical lymphocytic variants\n+- [x] Removed the misplaced parent-level synonym/xref usage\n+- [x] Committed only `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n+\n+Validation limitation:\n+- I could not run the required ODK normalization step (`make NORM`) or `robot convert` syntax validation in this environment because `docker` is not installed, and the repo's ODK wrapper depends on Docker. This is the only verification step I could not complete locally.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Summary:\n+- Created a distinct `lymphocytic hypophysitis` child term under `primary hypophysitis`.\n+- Removed `lymphocytic hypophysitis` and `autoimmune hypophysitis` from the parent term where they were modeled as exact synonyms.\n+- Reparented `adenohypophysitis`, `infundibulo-neurohypophysitis`, and `panhypophysitis` under `lymphocytic hypophysitis` to match the issue discussion and cited literature.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+Implemented the issue as a hierarchy correction rather than a synonym-only edit.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Added new term `MONDO:7770459` `lymphocytic hypophysitis`.\n+- Added a definition supported by `PMID:29547162` and `PMID:32965926`, both of which describe lymphocytic hypophysitis as the most frequent histopathologic subtype of primary hypophysitis.\n+- Moved the `NCIT:C132055` equivalence and the `autoimmune hypophysitis` synonym off `MONDO:0019835 primary hypophysitis` and onto the new `lymphocytic hypophysitis` term, because `NCIT:C132055` is `Autoimmune Hypophysitis` with exact synonym `Lymphocytic Hypophysitis`.\n+- Reparented these existing terms from `primary hypophysitis` to `lymphocytic hypophysitis`:\n+  - `MONDO:0019838` adenohypophysitis\n+  - `MONDO:0016534` infundibulo-neurohypophysitis\n+  - `MONDO:0019839` panhypophysitis\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue body and follow-up comment describe `primary hypophysitis` as the broader parent term.\n+- The cited sources support `lymphocytic hypophysitis` as a subtype, not as a synonym of the parent.\n+- Keeping `primary hypophysitis` aligned to its Orphanet-backed grouping concept while moving the NCIT mapping to the more specific child resolves the conceptual mismatch.\n+\n+Validation and research performed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Reviewed the cited NCBI Bookshelf page and PubMed entry for the Neurology India article.\n+- Verified that `NCIT:C132055` is labeled `Autoimmune Hypophysitis` and carries exact synonym `Lymphocytic Hypophysitis`.\n+- Verified that `MONDO:7770459` was unused before creating the new term.\n+- Checked the integrated stanzas in `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo` after check-in.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+- [x] Read issue context and comments\n+- [x] Reviewed cited references\n+- [x] Identified affected MONDO terms\n+- [x] Added a new subtype term with supporting references\n+- [x] Reparented existing anatomical lymphocytic variants\n+- [x] Removed the misplaced parent-level synonym/xref usage\n+- [x] Committed only `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n+\n+Validation limitation:\n+- I could not run the required ODK normalization step (`make NORM`) or `robot convert` syntax validation in this environment because `docker` is not installed, and the repo's ODK wrapper depends on Docker. This is the only verification step I could not complete locally.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","relativePath":"ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Summary:\n+- Created a distinct `lymphocytic hypophysitis` child term under `primary hypophysitis`.\n+- Removed `lymphocytic hypophysitis` and `autoimmune hypophysitis` from the parent term where they were modeled as exact synonyms.\n+- Reparented `adenohypophysitis`, `infundibulo-neurohypophysitis`, and `panhypophysitis` under `lymphocytic hypophysitis` to match the issue discussion and cited literature.\n","additions":6,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md","relativePath":"PR_COMMENTS.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+Implemented the issue as a hierarchy correction rather than a synonym-only edit.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Added new term `MONDO:7770459` `lymphocytic hypophysitis`.\n+- Added a definition supported by `PMID:29547162` and `PMID:32965926`, both of which describe lymphocytic hypophysitis as the most frequent histopathologic subtype of primary hypophysitis.\n+- Moved the `NCIT:C132055` equivalence and the `autoimmune hypophysitis` synonym off `MONDO:0019835 primary hypophysitis` and onto the new `lymphocytic hypophysitis` term, because `NCIT:C132055` is `Autoimmune Hypophysitis` with exact synonym `Lymphocytic Hypophysitis`.\n+- Reparented these existing terms from `primary hypophysitis` to `lymphocytic hypophysitis`:\n+  - `MONDO:0019838` adenohypophysitis\n+  - `MONDO:0016534` infundibulo-neurohypophysitis\n+  - `MONDO:0019839` panhypophysitis\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue body and follow-up comment describe `primary hypophysitis` as the broader parent term.\n+- The cited sources support `lymphocytic hypophysitis` as a subtype, not as a synonym of the parent.\n+- Keeping `primary hypophysitis` aligned to its Orphanet-backed grouping concept while moving the NCIT mapping to the more specific child resolves the conceptual mismatch.\n+\n+Validation and research performed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Reviewed the cited NCBI Bookshelf page and PubMed entry for the Neurology India article.\n+- Verified that `NCIT:C132055` is labeled `Autoimmune Hypophysitis` and carries exact synonym `Lymphocytic Hypophysitis`.\n+- Verified that `MONDO:7770459` was unused before creating the new term.\n+- Checked the integrated stanzas in `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo` after check-in.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+- [x] Read issue context and comments\n+- [x] Reviewed cited references\n+- [x] Identified affected MONDO terms\n+- [x] Added a new subtype term with supporting references\n+- [x] Reparented existing anatomical lymphocytic variants\n+- [x] Removed the misplaced parent-level synonym/xref usage\n+- [x] Committed only `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n+\n+Validation limitation:\n+- I could not run the required ODK normalization step (`make NORM`) or `robot convert` syntax validation in this environment because `docker` is not installed, and the repo's ODK wrapper depends on Docker. This is the only verification step I could not complete locally.\n","additions":34,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778979982345,"end":1778979982358}},"id":"prt_e337810a6001agtl2v2QeAaY7S","sessionID":"ses_1cc8acd6dffephn30ptdQ0bam5","messageID":"msg_e33780a58001iFnWnW1EFwsuyX"}}
